{
  "version": "0.2.0",
  "created": "2026-07-24",
  "notes": "Canonical RegisterBench pattern IDs mapped to each tool's own rule identifiers. 'map' values are the exact identifiers the tool emits (code track) or the rule, section or table headings in its ruleset files (prompt track). An empty list means the tool does not claim the pattern. v0.2.0 was produced by blind double-coding: for each of the 6 tool faces, two independent coders read only that tool's source (never this file), one working pattern-first and one rule-first, under a single written claim standard applied identically to every tool. Coders agreed on 172 of 174 cells (98.9%); the remaining cells were adjudicated against source. A later consistency review put three cells to a 3-adjudicator vote: two original decisions were upheld and one agreed cell (the-antislop, phr-novelty-inflation) was overturned to unclaimed, 0 votes to 3, so the same claim standard applies to the-antislop and stop-slop. Full per-cell evidence is in coding_record.json. v0.1.0 of this file was hand-authored by the same person who wrote the drafts and the scorer, and 15 of its 174 claim decisions differ in this version. Full-taxonomy recall counts unclaimed plants as misses; the claimed-only cut restricts to claimed plants. Crosswalk attribution grants span-level recall credit nowhere; it is used for claimed-only recall and for document-level rule credit.",
